		"outline": "a broad, rounded, airy irregular dome",
		"habit": "an ancient tree is 6 to 9 m tall and 8 to 12 m wide; width to height about 1.3 to 1.5 to 1. The crown is about two thirds of the height; the trunk up to the first limbs is about one third of the height. Trunk 1 to 2 m thick, gnarled, fluted, twisted in a spiral and often hollow. Widest at about two thirds of the height. Outline: a broad, rounded, airy irregular dome. One trunk, sometimes split into several parts by age.",
		"branching": "opposite, decussate on the young shoots. The old trunk opens into several crooked thick limbs that spread outward; outer twigs droop. Four or five orders from trunk to leaf.",
		"leaves": "simple, opposite, narrow lance-shaped, 4 to 10 cm long and 1 to 2 cm wide, about five to eight times as long as wide, widest at the middle, both ends tapered, the tip a small point. Margin entire. Stalk short, about 5 mm. Only the midrib is clear. Upper face dull grey-green; lower face silvery, covered in fine scales.",
